FILE: app/src/skip-ahead.ts
```ts
import { updateAnimationManager } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationManager } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function skipAhead(manager: AnimationManager, ms: number): void {
    const prev = manager.fixedDeltaMs;
    manager.fixedDeltaMs = 0;
    updateAnimationManager(manager, ms);
    manager.fixedDeltaMs = prev;
}
```

I created `src/skip-ahead.ts` which temporarily zeroes `fixedDeltaMs` so that `updateAnimationManager` honours the `ms` argument (per note 20, a fixed step would otherwise override it), calls the update once, then restores the original value so subsequent frames are unaffected. No uncertainty — the only non-obvious detail was the fixed-step override, and the notes make clear that `fixedDeltaMs = 0` disables it in favour of the passed delta.
